# Sovran Theme, Styling & Layout Rules

## Project Overview

This is a React Native/Expo app using NativeWind + Tailwind CSS with a comprehensive theming system. The app supports 30+ themes with dynamic color switching and background image themes.

## Directory Structure

- `components/ui/` - Basic UI components (Text, View, Button, Card, etc.)
- `components/blocks/` - Complex components (sheets, feeds, transactions, etc.)
- `providers/ThemeProvider.tsx` - Theme context and functions
- `themes.js` - Theme definitions with 0-950 color scales
- `helper/colorTheme.ts` - CSS variable mappings for NativeWind
- `redux/settings/` - Theme state management
- `app/settings-pages/theme.tsx` - Theme selection UI

## Theme System Rules

### Color System

- **ALWAYS** use theme functions for colors - never hardcode colors
- Use `getPrimaryColor(shade)` for theme-aware colors (0-950 scale)
- Use `getShadeColor(shade)` for brand/accent colors
- Use `getRedColor(shade)`, `getGreenColor(shade)`, `getPurpleColor(shade)` for semantic colors
- Import theme provider: `import { useTheme } from 'providers/ThemeProvider'`

### Component Styling

- **Text Component**: Use `Text` from `components/ui/Text` with theme colors
- **View Components**: Use `View`, `VStack`, `HStack` from `components/ui/View`
- **Buttons**: Use `Button` from `components/ui/Button` with variants (primary, secondary, dangerous)
- **Cards**: Use `Card` from `components/ui/Card` with variants (warning, info)

### Tailwind CSS Patterns

- Use CSS variables for colors: `className="bg-primary-800 text-primary-0"`
- Use `className` for layout, `style` prop for theme colors
- Common classes: `flex-1`, `p-4`, `rounded-lg`, `border-primary-100`

### Styling Best Practices

- Combine `className` for layout with `style` prop for theme colors
- Handle interactive states with theme colors
- Use blur effects with `blur={true}` and `blurIntensity={70}`
- Use ripple effects with `ripple={true}` on buttons

### Common Patterns

- Modal/Sheet: `className="bg-primary-900 rounded-t-3xl p-6"`
- List items: `className="flex-row items-center p-4 border-b border-primary-700"`
- Form inputs: `className="rounded-[32px] border border-primary-600 bg-primary-800"`

### Background Image Themes

- Use `setBackgroundImage()` for background themes (deepocean, cosmicpurple, mysticblue, royalpurple)
- Background images use the same color system as regular themes

### What NOT to Do

- Don't hardcode colors like `#1a1a1a` or `bg-gray-800`
- Don't use static Tailwind colors
- Don't forget to import `useTheme`
- Don't mix `style` and `className` incorrectly
- Don't assume color meanings - check theme definitions

### Testing

- Always test with multiple themes
- Use theme selector in settings to verify
- Test both light and dark themes
- Verify color contrast and readability
